    {
      "v": 2,
      "zh": "忽然有六个人从朝北的上门而来，各人手拿杀人的兵器；内中有一人身穿细麻衣，腰间带着墨盒子。他们进来，站在铜祭坛旁。",
      "en": "Next I noticed[NOTE:1] six men[NOTE:2] coming from the direction of the upper gate[NOTE:3] that faces north, each with his war club in his hand. Among them was a man dressed in linen with a writing kit[NOTE:4] at his side. They came and stood beside the bronze altar.",
      "notes": [
        "The word הִנֵּה (hinneh, traditionally “behold”) indicates becoming aware of something and has been translated here as a verb.",
        "The six men plus the scribe would equal seven, which was believed by the Babylonians to be the number of planetary deities.",
        "The upper gate was built by Jotham (2 Kgs 15:35).",
        "Or “a scribe’s inkhorn.” The Hebrew term occurs in the OT only in Ezek 9 and is believed to be an Egyptian loanword."
      ],
